zelda1-genesis - notices

The Legend of Zelda is (c) Nintendo. This project is not affiliated with or
endorsed by Nintendo. It contains no Nintendo ROM, graphics, music, level
data or program bytes: the converter derives them from a ROM you supply, on
your own computer. The game logic is reimplemented in C; like other
reimplementations it writes out some small lookup tables of the original
(item, enemy, palette and sound tables, about 2.5 KB in total as measured by
tools/builder/rom_bytes_scan.py).

Zelda Redux (ShadowOne333) is not included. You download its v3.3.3 patch
yourself; the converter applies it locally.
https://github.com/ShadowOne333/The-Legend-of-Zelda-Redux

Third-party components

- SGDK by Stephane Dallongeville, MIT License (git submodule sgdk/, which
  bundles the m68k-elf GCC toolchain and its licenses).
  https://github.com/Stephane-D/SGDK
- Zelda 1 disassembly by aldonunez: labels and comments (with this
  project's annotations) in reference/aldonunez_tpl/ and the RAM symbol
  files in reference/aldonunez/*.inc. Byte values are not included; the
  build restores them from your ROM. Upstream states no license.
  https://github.com/aldonunez/zelda1-disassembly
- Overworld and Underworld music: Genesis/Mega Drive covers by
  Inglebard, made in DefleMask Tracker, converted
  to XGM in data/audio_music/. The compositions are Koji Kondo's (Nintendo).
- Alternate Underworld music ("Zelda - Dungeon Jungle", Options > UW MUSIC):
  Genesis/Mega Drive cover by Cyberdeous, made in DefleMask Tracker,
  converted to XGM in data/audio_music/uw_theme_cyberdeous_xgm.c.
